{
  "schema": "6529-stream/governance-genesis/2",
  "description": "Example genesis configuration of the plain-core stack (ADR 0010). One network address holds every network role; operational keys are the only holders; no brake at launch. Genesis modules and minters are constructor arguments of Stream, Editions and Directory, so no bind is wired. Every waiting period in a permanent contract is a setting of the network, changed at once (NETWORK role, no role delay): moduleDelay 7 days, rescueDelay 14 days, rebindDelay 14 days, unclaimedPeriod 180 days at launch. Role delays are also the network's: a class's delay holds until a 7-day remap changes it. Every address is a placeholder. Generated by config/make_core_genesis.py.",
